# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working copy.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The repo is authored on Windows and runs on Linux:
# `apps/api/docker-entrypoint.sh` is the container's ENTRYPOINT, and a CRLF
# shebang makes Linux report `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` — so a fresh clone
# would build an image that cannot start. `ml/synthetic_dataset.csv` is
# regenerated in CI and compared with `git diff`, which a line-ending flip turns
# into a spurious "dataset is stale" failure.
#
# `eol=lf` (rather than bare `text=auto`) keeps the working tree LF too, so what
# is tested locally is byte-identical to what CI and the container see.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles are executed by Linux tooling — never CRLF.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Generated data compared byte-for-byte in CI.
*.csv           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
